extends RefCounted
const TEXT:="UNITS\nOne bot is placed in the arena by default.\nHover a unit to highlight it; click to focus it.\nDrag a unit to move it around the arena.\nReset position / Ctrl+R: restore original placement.\nAlt+arrows: nudge the selected unit (outside clip editing).\n[ / ]: switch the focused unit.\nF: focus the camera on the selected character.\n\nTAKE CONTROL\nSelect a bot, then click Take Control in the bottom bar.\nWASD moves, Shift sprints, Space jumps. Wheel zooms the camera; middle/right-drag or arrows orbit. −/+ zoom, Home resets camera. Gamepad: left stick move, right stick orbit, R3 zoom out, A jump, X/RB timeline, B release.\nClick the arena or use Play to perform the current timeline once.\nOther added units are contact-based practice targets.\nBackspace restores test units; Escape or Release Control returns to editing.\n\nPREVIEW & PLAY\n▶ beside an animation: preview its whole body once on the focused unit. The timeline stays unchanged.\nDrag an animation onto a timeline track, then use the bottom ▶ to play it on the focused unit.\nEVERYTHING affects the whole body; other tracks affect that body part. Higher numbers win overlapping pose conflicts. Jump height continues beneath other poses.\nOverlap a backflip with jump airtime, then add a higher-priority slash on LEFT ARM.\n\nEDIT CLIPS\nDrag the middle: move the clip.\nDrag an edge: stretch/shrink playback (changes speed).\nShift-drag an edge: cut/trim (keeps speed).\nShift-click inside a clip: split at that point.\nSelect a clip, place the playhead, then press S: cut there.\nRight-click a clip or press Delete: remove it.\nShaded time is beyond Length and will not play.\n\nSHORTCUTS\nCtrl+Z: undo an animation or timeline edit.\nCtrl+Y: redo.\nCtrl+C: copy the selected clip.\nCtrl+P (or Ctrl+V): paste at the playhead.\nWith a clip focused: S splits at the playhead.\nAlt+← / →: trim the end by one frame.\nCtrl+Alt+← / →: trim the start.\nShift+← / →: stretch/shrink by one frame.\nWith the ruler focused: ← / → seeks one frame; Shift seeks ten; Home / End goes to start/end.\n\nPANELS\nDrag a divider to resize the panels.\nDouble-click a divider to reset it.\nWith a divider focused: arrows resize by 6 px; Shift+arrows resize by 24 px.\nYour panel sizes are remembered.\nUse − to collapse a side panel and + to reopen it.\n\nJUMP STAMINA\nStamina depletion controls jump height and airtime. Extending a jump automatically increases its stamina requirement, up to 100. Put Jump on EVERYTHING and a jab on its arm track to combine them. At equal priority the specific body-part track wins.\n\nPANEL ZOOM\nCtrl+mouse wheel over a panel: shrink or enlarge its text and controls. On Spells, middle-mouse drag up/down also zooms; on Store, hold Ctrl and middle-drag up/down. Each panel zooms independently. Time zoom − / + spreads or compresses seconds without changing the animation. Ctrl+Shift+wheel over Timeline changes time zoom. Ctrl+wheel changes panel text and control sizing, including Timeline. Time zoom is saved independently. Ctrl+- / Ctrl+= works over a panel; Ctrl+0 resets it. Zoom levels are saved with your layout.\n\nSTORE & PERSONAL LIBRARY\nSearch words or quoted phrases. Combine tag:arm body:head state:airborne source:ual2 author:name; use -tag:fall to exclude. Filters cover body part, air/ground and Available/Taken/Blocked/All items. Drag a Store animation onto a category folder or anywhere in the open category list, including its blank space. Drag the Store title to move it; drag any border or corner to resize the actual window. Taken items hide from Available. Duplicate names receive (1), (2), etc. Use the pencil beside an animation to rename it; its original source and credits remain in metadata. Block hides unwanted items; switch to Blocked to undo it. Source metadata and the full credit history are retained with every animation. New changes are automatically credited to foreandr while preserving prior contributors."
